const body = `<h1>1.5a — Tip Calculator (Build Together)</h1>

<p>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Basic Application. The Slot Machine used Math.random()
    for game logic; the Tip Calculator uses arithmetic and the three-step pattern
    for real-world math. Same skeleton, different meat.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>The Goal</h3>

    <p>Given a bill amount and a tip percentage, calculate and display the tip and total.</p>

    <pre><code><span class="output">===== TIP CALCULATOR =====
Bill:  $45.5
Tip:   $9.1
Total: $54.6
==========================</span></code></pre>

    <h3>Iteration 1: Declare the Data</h3>

    <p>Create a new class called <code>TipCalculator</code> with a <code>main</code> method.
    Declare four variables:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>The starting bill amount — set it to <code>45.50</code></li>
        <li>The tip percentage — set it to <code>20</code></li>
        <li>The calculated tip amount — don't set a value yet</li>
        <li>The final total amount — don't set a value yet</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <p>
            What data type should you use for these variables? Why is
            <code>int</code> a bad choice for money?
        </p>
    </div>

    <h3>Iteration 2: The Math Trap</h3>

    <p>Now calculate the tip. 20 percent means 20 ÷ 100.</p>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Bug Hunt: The Zero Dollar Tip</h3>
        <p>Add this calculation to your code:</p>
        <pre><code>tip = billAmount * (tipPercent / 100);
System.out.println("Debug Tip: " + tip);</code></pre>
        <p>Run it. The output is <code>Debug Tip: 0.0</code>. Why does the tip
        come out as zero? What do you think Java did with the division? How have
        you solved a similar problem before?</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it.</strong> The tip should be 20% of 45.50, which is 9.10.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Iteration 3: Display the Receipt</h3>

    <p>Once the math is fixed, calculate <code>total</code> (bill + tip). Then
    replace your debug print with a nicely formatted receipt matching the Goal
    output above.</p>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Compare this program to the Slot Machine. What's the same?
                What's different?</li>
            <li>Why does the three-step pattern work for BOTH programs when
                they do such different things?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/tip-calculator.html">Tip Calculator Walkthrough</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/arithmetic.html">Arithmetic &amp; Operators</a> — the integer division trap</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/three-step-pattern.html">Three-Step Pattern</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
